      "body": "## Summary\n\nAdapters trained with `bias=\"lora_only\"` or `bias=\"all\"` pass validation, and their bias tensors enter projection normalization as LoRA matrix weights.\n\nReject these adapters in the shared validator before changing configuration or loading weights. The error identifies the adapter and asks for one trained with `bias=\"none\"`. Missing bias and `bias=\"none\"` remain supported.\n\nRefs #41828.\n\n## Verification\n\nUsing the real CPU adapter loaders with saved safetensors and tensor input:\n\n| Adapter | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `bias=\"all\"` or `\"lora_only\"` | Success, with a 1D `qkv_proj.bias` among normalized matrix weights | Rejected; configuration and registry unchanged |\n| `bias=\"none\"` | Success | Success, with identical matrices |\n\n- The new regression failed before the patch and passes afterward. It covers file, tensor, and initial adapter loading, supported defaults, and state preservation.\n- Related CPU tests: 11 passed, with 8 subtests.\n- Changed-file pre-commit hooks passed.\n",
